// ============================================================================
//  zm_qol wpnfix donor  -  built by build_wpnfix.bat, loaded FIRST by build_ff.
//
//  Sole purpose: supply the 1911 weapon defs from RETAIL instead of from
//  zone_source\base\mod.ff. The donor's copies name fire aliases that exist
//  nowhere in BO2 (wpn_m1911_*, wpn_mc96_*), so the guns were silent; retail's
//  copies name wpn_1911_*, which every map bank declares and which the user's
//  sound pack replaces. The Linker is first-load-wins, so the only way to beat
//  the donor is to supply the name from a zone loaded ahead of it.
// ============================================================================
>game,T6

//  m1911_zm IS BACK HERE (v2.15.40 took it out; user call 2026-09-23 puts it
//  back). It asks retail's wpn_1911_fire_plr, and the 11-row wpn_m1911_* chain
//  has been dropped from soundbank\mod.all.aliases.additions.csv. This is the
//  "reversible in one line" the note below used to describe, taken.
//
//  WHY. v2.15.40 gave the M1911 the UNSHARED alias wpn_m1911_fire_plr and put
//  the shot inside mod.all. Those bytes were the user's sound pack's M1911
//  remaster, so EVERY player heard the pack whether or not they installed it.
//  Measured 2026-09-23: mod.all.sabl id db0e8cef is byte-identical (73,728 B,
//  sha1 01c9d14e27...) to what the pack writes over retail's fnp45 shot in
//  cmn_root; retail's own is 176,704 B. A private alias can never be reached
//  by the pack, because the pack only ever replaces payloads behind RETAIL
//  names in the stock banks.
//
//  So the alias has to be retail's. wpn_1911_fire_plr resolves out of
//  cmn_root.all.sabl, and Plutonium loads that from storage\t6\zone when the
//  pack is installed and from the game's own sound\ folder when it is not
//  (proven in console_zm.log, which prints the full path of every bank).
//  Stock by default, pack overrides on install - which is the requirement.
//
//  🛑 THE COST, STATED PLAINLY: wpn_1911_fire_plr is MAP-DEPENDENT. zmb_tomb
//  points it at wpn_mauser_fire, every other map bank at wpn_fnp45_fire_plr.
//  Treyarch could share the name because retail never lets the M1911 onto
//  Origins; this mod's starting-pistol row does. So on Origins - classic and
//  survival, Crazy Place included - the M1911 fires the Mauser's shot. There
//  is no third way: wpn_fnp45_fire_plr is MP-only and is declared by NO
//  zombies map bank, so it cannot be borrowed to dodge tomb's mapping.
//  To go back to a correct-everywhere M1911 that the pack cannot touch,
//  delete the weapon,m1911_zm line below and restore the 11 rows.
//
//  The two upgraded halves stay on retail's wpn_1911_*_pap names either way -
//  Mustang & Sally are untouched everywhere.
weapon,m1911_zm
weapon,m1911_upgraded_zm
weapon,m1911lh_upgraded_zm

//  v2.8.9 - c96_zm IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. User report 2026-08-30: the Mauser
//  has the wrong shooting sound on every map except Origins. Retail's c96_zm asks
//  for wpn_1911_fire_plr, and that alias is MAP-DEPENDENT: zmb_tomb points it at
//  wpn_mauser_fire, every other map bank points it at wpn_fnp45_fire_plr - the
//  M1911's shot. Treyarch could share the name because retail never lets the
//  Mauser leave Origins; this mod does. So the fix is the opposite of the 1911's:
//  let zone_source\base\mod.ff keep supplying c96_zm, whose fire aliases are the
//  UNSHARED wpn_mc96_fire_{plr,npc}, and declare that family in mod.all. Measured:
//  the donor's c96_zm differs from retail's in exactly 2 of 2055 fields (the two
//  fire aliases), and its 11-row wpn_mc96_* chain is a rename of retail Origins'
//  wpn_1911_* chain - same payloads, same secondary wiring. No stock bank declares
//  any wpn_mc96_* name, so nothing is shadowed.
